# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

This project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/).

---

## [v0.2.0] - 2026-06-06

### Added
- OAuth login with GitHub via Laravel Socialite
- OAuth login with Google via Laravel Socialite
- `SocialiteController` with provider validation
- Migration for `provider`, `provider_id`, `provider_token` columns on users table
- OAuth buttons on login and register views
- `.env.example` variables for GitHub and Google credentials
- Graceful fallback for users without public name on GitHub (uses nickname)

## OAuth local development note

Google OAuth does not accept `.test` domains. For local testing use:

```env
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://127.0.0.1:80/auth/google/callback
```

Or use [ngrok](https://ngrok.com) to expose your local app with a public domain.

GitHub OAuth works fine with `.test` domains.

---

## [v0.0.1] - 2026-06-06

### Added
- Laravel 13 base installation
- Laravel Fortify as auth engine
- Livewire 3
- Tailwind CSS 4
- User registration
- Login / Logout
- Forgot password
- Reset password (with log driver for local testing)
- Email verification
- Protected dashboard route
- SQLite as default database
- MIT License
- README with setup instructions
- CONTRIBUTING guide

### Notes
- Fortify is used as auth engine while Breeze/Jetstream don't officially support Laravel 13
- No OAuth, 2FA, or roles in this version — see roadmap in CONTRIBUTING.md

---

